Ticket **#4471** was marked known as one parser bug. The merged reports hold **two**
causes. This page records the split and the desk tickets opened for each.

<Callout>
Not one issue. Two causes under the same merge: <code>parser</code> (379) and
<code>hint</code> (33).
</Callout>

## What was merged

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Desk tickets

| cause | reports | ticket |
| --- | ---: | --- |
| `parser` — shared parser reads month-first for day-first tenants | 379 | [#1](https://github.com/mateusz-c/mega-course-lesson/issues/1) |
| `hint` — booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` while the form reads day-first | 33 | [#2](https://github.com/mateusz-c/mega-course-lesson/issues/2) |

## Why the merge was wrong

Decision [0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject alone. Many
subjects look like the same date bug, so intake filed both causes into #4471. The
cause depends on the tenant's locale and booking form (`#lib/kb/causes`), not the
subject line.

## Next

Engineering owns two fixes. Keep #4471 closed as a merge artifact; work the two
tickets above.

